  "residue": {
    "_note": "The irreducible memorize-list (heart words): words the simple productive rules cannot resolve from letters alone. Consulted by the engine BEFORE applying an ambiguous rule, so the RULE stays one sentence and these stay a plain list \u2014 not rule clauses.",
    "edNotSuffix": {
      "_rule": "In these words the final 'ed' is NOT the non-syllabic -ed suffix; the 'e' is a real vowel and its own syllable (hun-dred, sa-cred, na-ked). Skip the -ed rule for them. They are unresolvable from letters (naked vs baked, jagged vs jogged).",
